WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.740
What do we say when somebody helps us?

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:08.528
In Korean, thank you is gomapseumnida.

00:00:08.928 --> 00:00:10.804
고맙습니다  (go-map-seum-ni-da) - Korean

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.752
In English, we simply say thank you.

00:00:17.152 --> 00:00:18.740
THANK YOU  (thank-you) - English

00:00:20.948 --> 00:00:23.864
In Japanese, thank you is arigato.

00:00:24.264 --> 00:00:25.924
ありがとう  (a-ri-ga-toh) - Japanese

00:00:28.116 --> 00:00:32.508
In Chinese, thank you is xiexie.

00:00:32.908 --> 00:00:34.208
谢谢  (shieh-shieh) - Chinese

00:00:36.276 --> 00:00:38.868
In French, thank you is merci.

00:00:39.268 --> 00:00:40.820
MERCI  (mehr-see) - Francais

00:00:42.996 --> 00:00:46.128
In Russian, thank you is spasibo.

00:00:46.528 --> 00:00:48.404
СПАСИБО  (spa-see-ba) - Russian

00:00:50.676 --> 00:00:53.628
In Arabic, thank you is shukran.

00:00:54.028 --> 00:00:55.616
شكرا  (shuk-ran) - Arabic

00:00:57.748 --> 00:01:01.888
Thank you in seven languages. Shall we say them together?

